      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not delay seeking emergency medical attention if you cannot shake after eating juice, as moderate hypoglycemia can worsen into severe neuroglycopenia which is life-threatening. While 15–20 grams of carbohydrate (like one glass of juice or three glucose tablets) is typically the standard first treatment, you should reassess your blood sugar and re-treat in 15 minutes if symptoms persist rather than waiting indefinitely. Please call your doctor immediately if you have been injected with long-acting insulin, as they can provide you with specific glucose calculations tailored to your current situation at no cost. I am staying with you until they can get in touch with you.",
